1
00:01:02,331 --> 00:01:03,451
Sorry!

2
00:01:03,541 --> 00:01:06,171
I missed the vital spot! I'll put you at ease--

3
00:01:06,251 --> 00:01:08,631
Askeladd...

4
00:01:10,291 --> 00:01:12,841
I wanted to be friends with you...

5
00:01:18,551 --> 00:01:20,391
Yeah. Bjorn...

6
00:01:21,351 --> 00:01:22,721
You...

7
00:01:23,771 --> 00:01:25,811
You are my only...

8
00:01:27,101 --> 00:01:28,231
friend.

9
00:01:38,661 --> 00:01:41,031
Send me off...

10
00:02:00,721 --> 00:02:04,061
Well, then, sorry to keep you waiting, kid.

11
00:02:05,351 --> 00:02:06,521
Come.

12
00:02:11,611 --> 00:02:13,111
I'll play with you.

13
00:03:55,881 --> 00:03:58,301
LONE WOLF

14
00:04:08,391 --> 00:04:09,931
Damn.

15
00:04:10,021 --> 00:04:11,561
He's acting different than usual.

16
00:04:14,901 --> 00:04:18,821
So? Who do you think is going to win, prince?

17
00:04:18,901 --> 00:04:20,731
Want to make a bet?

18
00:04:20,821 --> 00:04:22,781
I don't care who wins.

19
00:04:22,861 --> 00:04:24,861
I'll stop the duel before someone dies.

20
00:04:25,491 --> 00:04:27,781
You're no fun!

21
00:04:28,031 --> 00:04:32,911
You don't get to see duels
between such skilled warriors every day.

22
00:04:35,121 --> 00:04:38,881
Well, then, which one do you think is stronger?

23
00:04:39,801 --> 00:04:43,381
Me? Well...

24
00:04:44,471 --> 00:04:48,101
I guess Askeladd. I bet one pound of silver on him.

25
00:04:48,181 --> 00:04:50,681
I'm not going to make a bet.
Why do you think so?

26
00:04:52,931 --> 00:04:55,441
Just a feeling. It's his aura.

27
00:04:56,481 --> 00:04:59,651
Thorfinn defeated you.

28
00:04:59,731 --> 00:05:01,691
Is Askeladd even better than that?

29
00:05:01,781 --> 00:05:05,361
You. Prince. Who do you think I am?

30
00:05:05,451 --> 00:05:11,201
There's no way that I'm the weakest one
out of us three. Right?

31
00:05:13,621 --> 00:05:17,751
It's not that simple to tell who's stronger
and who's weaker.

32
00:05:17,831 --> 00:05:22,381
Sometimes you win, and sometimes you lose.
It's not easy to rank people. That's the fun part.

33
00:05:24,131 --> 00:05:25,131
I'm not interested.

34
00:05:26,221 --> 00:05:27,931
You must be a woman.

35
00:05:30,891 --> 00:05:33,641
What's wrong, Thorfinn? Come.

36
00:05:34,681 --> 00:05:37,021
I want to finish this before the snow gets worse.

37
00:05:43,981 --> 00:05:45,821
I have no choice.

38
00:05:53,541 --> 00:05:56,411
Look. Now, it's easier to attack me, right?

39
00:05:58,791 --> 00:06:00,831
Come, boy.

40
00:06:16,851 --> 00:06:17,851
Right?

41
00:06:20,521 --> 00:06:25,191
You still don't understand why it turns out like this?

42
00:06:41,041 --> 00:06:45,551
I take back what I said just now.
This isn't a duel.

43
00:06:45,631 --> 00:06:49,971
Askeladd knows Thorfinn's habits.
He can see through his cover.

44
00:06:51,141 --> 00:06:54,931
These two must have dueled many times.
What's the reason for the duel?

45
00:06:56,011 --> 00:06:58,481
I don't know. No one told me.

46
00:07:03,481 --> 00:07:05,151
Unbelievable.

47
00:07:05,231 --> 00:07:07,281
You never learn, kid.

48
00:07:08,781 --> 00:07:11,361
Did you get full of yourself after you beat Thorkell?

49
00:07:16,831 --> 00:07:19,291
I'm sick of you.

50
00:07:21,621 --> 00:07:23,461
Stop! That's enough!

51
00:07:27,341 --> 00:07:30,471
Did you think you could beat me
with only one arm?

52
00:07:34,511 --> 00:07:36,221
Come on.

53
00:07:36,311 --> 00:07:39,141
Today, I'm feeling damn good.

54
00:07:40,141 --> 00:07:41,311
Stop!

55
00:07:49,651 --> 00:07:52,281
Stop. He's passed out.

56
00:07:52,361 --> 00:07:53,951
You win.

57
00:07:54,031 --> 00:07:58,541
You're really going to stop them?

58
00:07:58,621 --> 00:08:01,161
Thorfinn! Hey! Thorfinn!

59
00:08:09,251 --> 00:08:12,761
Do you understand? The duel is over.

60
00:08:12,841 --> 00:08:14,471
You lost.

61
00:08:19,471 --> 00:08:22,061
Enough. It's over now.

62
00:08:22,141 --> 00:08:23,311
You bastard!

63
00:08:23,391 --> 00:08:25,811
You passed out.

64
00:08:25,901 --> 00:08:27,561
He already delivered the deathblow.

65
00:08:31,651 --> 00:08:34,321
Start over again once your right arm has healed.

66
00:08:37,661 --> 00:08:39,911
It will end the same way
even after your arm heals.

67
00:08:39,991 --> 00:08:42,041
It's not because of your wound.

68
00:08:42,121 --> 00:08:44,711
You're an idiot who loses because he's an idiot.

69
00:08:45,501 --> 00:08:49,211
Normally, you know how to think while you fight.

70
00:08:50,501 --> 00:08:54,341
But once you lose your temper,
it all goes to waste.

71
00:08:55,471 --> 00:08:59,641
I can tell from where you're looking
that you're going after my neck.

72
00:09:03,061 --> 00:09:06,811
Losing your temper, shouting loudly,

73
00:09:06,901 --> 00:09:10,151
and waving your sword around
is how an idiot fights.

74
00:09:10,231 --> 00:09:12,821
Unbelievable. Everyone's the same.

75
00:09:12,901 --> 00:09:15,151
There's no beauty in it.

76
00:09:16,741 --> 00:09:19,451
Bjorn is right.

77
00:09:19,531 --> 00:09:22,041
I hate warriors.

78
00:09:23,331 --> 00:09:27,081
Especially Norse warriors, Vikings.

79
00:09:30,041 --> 00:09:33,761
The first man I ever killed was also a Norse warrior.

80
00:09:33,841 --> 00:09:36,381
He was not a beautiful man.

81
00:09:40,931 --> 00:09:42,681
He was my father.

82
00:09:45,391 --> 00:09:47,271
Kid...

83
00:09:47,351 --> 00:09:49,941
I'm going to tell you something for future reference.

84
00:09:51,271 --> 00:09:55,321
I'm going to tell you how to kill someone you hate.

85
00:10:08,501 --> 00:10:10,381
All right!

86
00:10:10,461 --> 00:10:12,921
-I'm getting old.
-Watch out behind you.

87
00:10:17,551 --> 00:10:21,011
My mother was a slave.

88
00:10:24,851 --> 00:10:28,521
My mother was sick and couldn't work.

89
00:10:30,561 --> 00:10:32,861
So, ever since I was old enough to remember,

90
00:10:32,941 --> 00:10:35,481
I was working in the blacksmith's shop and the stable.

91
00:10:38,951 --> 00:10:41,451
My body was always covered in

92
00:10:41,531 --> 00:10:46,041
ash, coal, or horse manure,
and was always white or black.

93
00:10:46,121 --> 00:10:48,121
They gave me the nickname "Askeladd."

94
00:10:50,211 --> 00:10:52,211
It means "covered in ash."

95
00:10:53,671 --> 00:10:56,711
Olaf has returned!

96
00:10:56,801 --> 00:10:59,721
He was victorious again!

97
00:11:05,931 --> 00:11:08,731
My father was from a powerful family in Jutland.

98
00:11:08,811 --> 00:11:12,311
-Olaf!
-Welcome back, Olaf!

99
00:11:12,401 --> 00:11:15,731
He loved booze, women and killing people.

100
00:11:15,821 --> 00:11:18,241
He was a Viking,
just like those you'd find anywhere else.

101
00:11:19,401 --> 00:11:24,071
I heard he had lots of kids like me
with random women here and there.

102
00:11:24,161 --> 00:11:28,871
But he only named the older kids
he had with his legal wife.

103
00:11:31,961 --> 00:11:36,501
He probably didn't even know
what his other kids looked like.

104
00:11:40,971 --> 00:11:42,511
I heard that my mother

105
00:11:42,591 --> 00:11:45,891
was one of my father's favorite slaves
when she was younger.

106
00:11:46,971 --> 00:11:50,891
But after she fell ill, he treated her like a dog.

107
00:11:52,231 --> 00:11:55,901
For me, life had always been hard.

108
00:11:55,981 --> 00:11:59,071
But it was different for my mother.

109
00:12:03,241 --> 00:12:08,661
My mother often told me about
the hero Artorius, one of our ancestors.

110
00:12:08,741 --> 00:12:11,461
She told the same story many times.

111
00:12:13,171 --> 00:12:15,921
The legend was about a general
who protected my mother's homeland

112
00:12:16,001 --> 00:12:19,461
from being invaded by savages 500 years ago.

113
00:12:21,511 --> 00:12:25,551
My mother believed the legend's prophecy
that the hero would be resurrected.

114
00:12:25,641 --> 00:12:31,101
She believed that he would return
to free her from illness and enslavement.

115
00:12:33,981 --> 00:12:36,271
She kept repeating it.

116
00:12:36,351 --> 00:12:38,361
So, I started to believe it, too.

117
00:12:39,651 --> 00:12:42,071
She said that far to the west,

118
00:12:42,151 --> 00:12:46,201
in a land across the sea
where ordinary people cannot reach,

119
00:12:47,661 --> 00:12:51,371
there lies a paradise where the hero Artorius lives.

120
00:12:57,421 --> 00:13:03,131
A paradise, where peace,
prosperity and eternal life is promised.

121
00:13:05,801 --> 00:13:11,061
The hero is still there now, healing his battle wounds.

122
00:13:12,811 --> 00:13:18,691
Someday, he will come
leading an army to slay the savages

123
00:13:18,771 --> 00:13:21,021
and conquer the world.

124
00:13:22,151 --> 00:13:26,151
My mother's family kept waiting for him.

125
00:13:29,871 --> 00:13:31,791
They waited for 500 years.

126
00:13:33,751 --> 00:13:37,171
The hero hasn't appeared yet.

127
00:13:41,091 --> 00:13:43,761
But just think about it.

128
00:13:43,841 --> 00:13:48,511
If our ancestor really was living in such a nice place,

129
00:13:48,591 --> 00:13:51,761
he'd never choose to come back to a world like this.

130
00:13:57,021 --> 00:14:02,691
When I was 11, my mother's heart finally snapped.

131
00:14:11,871 --> 00:14:12,871
Mother!

132
00:14:25,301 --> 00:14:29,761
Of all the things that could happen,
she thought that my father, who was just passing by,

133
00:14:29,841 --> 00:14:32,681
was the hero Artorius.

134
00:14:47,151 --> 00:14:49,111
I realized in an instant.

135
00:14:50,781 --> 00:14:54,491
If Artorius wasn't going to
come save my mother in that moment,

136
00:14:54,581 --> 00:14:57,451
then he's never going to come.

137
00:14:58,581 --> 00:15:00,751
Do you understand, kids?

138
00:15:01,831 --> 00:15:04,251
Someone must do it.

139
00:15:04,341 --> 00:15:08,051
A person, not a hero, and not a god.

140
00:15:23,311 --> 00:15:25,361
It's weird.

141
00:15:25,441 --> 00:15:29,901
I had never used a sword before
but it felt right in my hands.

142
00:15:29,991 --> 00:15:32,241
I knew how to swing it.

143
00:15:33,571 --> 00:15:38,701
I thought of it as proof that I had the blood of
that damn bastard flowing through my veins.

144
00:15:38,791 --> 00:15:40,751
I'm so ashamed.

145
00:15:40,831 --> 00:15:42,871
It makes me want to cry.

146
00:15:55,301 --> 00:15:57,141
You.

147
00:15:57,221 --> 00:15:59,431
Are you her child?

148
00:16:03,811 --> 00:16:05,691
Are you my child?

149
00:16:08,071 --> 00:16:09,231
Yes.

150
00:16:20,371 --> 00:16:22,501
You have potential.

151
00:16:22,581 --> 00:16:24,371
You live in the hall starting today.

152
00:16:27,501 --> 00:16:31,551
I knew he wasn't someone who an 11-year-old could kill.

153
00:16:32,921 --> 00:16:37,221
But I succeeded in getting my father to notice me.

154
00:16:39,511 --> 00:16:42,061
I behaved myself in the hall.

155
00:16:42,141 --> 00:16:45,601
I didn't slack off in my training
for the military arts or horsemanship.

156
00:16:45,691 --> 00:16:48,981
I even got along well with my half-brothers.

157
00:16:56,701 --> 00:16:58,281
Good job, Askeladd.

158
00:16:59,741 --> 00:17:03,501
I always made sure I showed respect to my father.

159
00:17:16,681 --> 00:17:22,771
I was a loyal son and didn't forget
that he saved me from my life as a slave.

160
00:17:22,851 --> 00:17:28,981
Before long, everyone
started to accept me as my father's son.

161
00:17:32,361 --> 00:17:36,071
I worked on it for two years.

162
00:17:51,541 --> 00:17:54,051
I was after two things.

163
00:17:54,131 --> 00:17:57,931
I wanted to catch him with his guard down,
and I wanted the right to inherit his property.

164
00:18:02,391 --> 00:18:05,431
I wish you could have seen it.

165
00:18:05,521 --> 00:18:08,311
His face had this look, like he was asking, "Why?"

166
00:18:14,071 --> 00:18:16,531
I used my brother's sword.

167
00:18:16,611 --> 00:18:19,861
I chose someone who didn't
get along with my father and stole his sword.

168
00:18:21,031 --> 00:18:26,701
My other brothers thought
he was the one who did it and hanged him.

169
00:18:26,791 --> 00:18:29,121
They're so simple-minded.

170
00:18:31,041 --> 00:18:33,131
They're stupid and filthy.

171
00:18:33,211 --> 00:18:36,711
The have nothing except for their own greed.

172
00:18:39,051 --> 00:18:43,971
People without beauty like them
started popping up everywhere

173
00:18:44,061 --> 00:18:46,311
and throwing their weight around.

174
00:18:46,391 --> 00:18:48,691
There's no end to it, no matter how many I kill.

175
00:18:49,941 --> 00:18:55,151
I don't care whether it's Artorius, Ragnarok,
or the Last Judgment.

176
00:18:55,231 --> 00:18:58,531
If you're really going to come,
then you'd better hurry.

177
00:19:00,991 --> 00:19:06,161
Well, when that happens, I bet they're not going to
let me keep on living either though.

178
00:19:09,911 --> 00:19:13,841
Well, that was a long story. Anyway, Thorfinn...

179
00:19:15,001 --> 00:19:19,131
you still can't even kill me
even though it's been 10 years.

180
00:19:19,221 --> 00:19:21,261
That means you're an idiot.

181
00:19:25,601 --> 00:19:27,181
Shut up!

182
00:19:27,271 --> 00:19:28,311
I'm...

183
00:19:28,391 --> 00:19:30,811
I'm going to kill you, no matter what happens!

184
00:19:31,731 --> 00:19:33,611
I'm going to kill you, no matter what!

185
00:19:40,071 --> 00:19:41,281
Come on.

186
00:19:42,611 --> 00:19:44,911
You're still saying that? Right after what I told you?

187
00:19:46,581 --> 00:19:50,161
You're just like a dog chasing after food.

188
00:19:52,541 --> 00:19:56,381
I really am thankful for all your hard work.

189
00:19:56,461 --> 00:20:00,131
All I have to do is put on an act
having these duels with you.

190
00:20:00,211 --> 00:20:03,931
And then you'd go run off
and even fight someone like Thorkell.

191
00:20:05,351 --> 00:20:08,511
You're a useful kid.

192
00:20:11,981 --> 00:20:12,981
Unbelievable.

193
00:20:14,561 --> 00:20:17,691
I must thank Thors, too.

194
00:20:27,331 --> 00:20:28,581
Wait.

195
00:20:30,161 --> 00:20:31,661
Wait!

196
00:20:31,751 --> 00:20:33,001
Stop.

197
00:20:33,081 --> 00:20:37,671
Shut up! Shut up! Shut up! Be quiet!

198
00:20:37,751 --> 00:20:39,341
Now is the time to heal your wounds.

199
00:20:40,511 --> 00:20:41,971
I said wait.

200
00:20:45,301 --> 00:20:46,391
Won't you stop?

201
00:20:53,431 --> 00:20:56,601
How pathetic.

202
00:20:59,981 --> 00:21:03,991
Oh, dear. You're stiff now, Bjorn.

203
00:21:13,291 --> 00:21:15,711
Why me?

204
00:21:19,421 --> 00:21:22,711
You're the hero's descendant, Askeladd.

205
00:21:22,801 --> 00:21:23,921
And you're quick-witted.

206
00:21:25,221 --> 00:21:29,641
Don't you want to become the king yourself
and change the world?

207
00:21:32,771 --> 00:21:34,771
You're joking, right?

208
00:21:34,851 --> 00:21:36,891
Weren't you listening just now?

209
00:21:41,401 --> 00:21:43,741
You're more suited to be the king.

210
00:21:44,781 --> 00:21:46,901
More than me or King Sweyn.

211
00:21:48,071 --> 00:21:50,411
I can tell by looking at your face.

212
00:21:54,001 --> 00:21:57,081
I'm just a Viking.
